{:id "0023-credits-fix"
 :title "Credits roll as credits: one line per line, focus inside, Escape closes"
 :lupa/deps #{"0020-credits-roll"}
 :lupa/area :ui
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The credits roll shipped by 0020 passes its unit tests but renders
        wrong (foreman's browser check, 2026-10-21): the lines run together
        ('FIRST LIGHTBENSCOUT · AGENT OF BEN2 LINES EXCHANGED…') with the
        blank lines lost; focus never enters the dialog, so Escape does
        nothing (the autofocus attribute only works on page load, never on
        elements inserted later); and the End scene and Close buttons are
        unstyled browser defaults. Fix all three, and make the e2e smoke
        test exercise the credits so this cannot regress unseen."
 :scope ["public/css/halfahead.css" "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc"
         "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc" "src/halfahead/app.cljs"
         "src/halfahead/app/enrich.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/enrich_test.cljc"
         "e2e/smoke.mjs"]
 :design "Line breaks: the performed copy and the sr-only copy of the
          credits keep the text's newlines (white-space: pre-line or
          pre-wrap on the credits body; each newline-terminated segment
          already ends with its newline character). Blank lines remain
          visible as space.
          Focus: replace autofocus with a Replicant life-cycle hook expressed
          as data on the dialog, e.g. {:replicant/on-mount [[:dom/focus]]}.
          The shell's dispatch receives life-cycle triggers with the DOM
          node (:replicant/node); when an action is [:dom/focus] it calls
          .focus on that node (the dialog has tabindex -1) and does nothing
          else — no core change. Escape: event data in hiccup cannot inspect the key,
          so the dialog's keydown emits [[:scene/key]] and
          halfahead.app.enrich maps it the way it maps the composer's Enter:
          key \"Escape\" -> [[:scene/dismissed]], any other key -> [] (and
          prevent-default? is false for it).
          Overlay: fixed to the viewport, the paper colour, the credits
          centred in a column in the label type, generous line height; the
          Close button and the End scene button styled like the other quiet
          controls (outlined, label type), with visible focus.
          e2e/smoke.mjs: a fifth step after the reduced-motion step: click
          End scene; wait 5.5 s; assert the dialog exists and has focus
          within it; assert the credits lines are on different rows (the
          bounding boxes of the 'BEN' line and the 'HALF AHEAD' line differ
          in y by more than 40px); screenshot out/e2e/credits.png; press
          Escape; assert the dialog is gone."
 :acceptance
 ["`bb e2e` passes with the new credits step, and the final message lists
   out/e2e/credits.png"
  "View tests: the dialog carries the on-mount focus hook as data,
   tabindex -1, and keydown [[:scene/key]]; no autofocus attribute remains"
  "Enrich tests: [:scene/key] with key Escape -> [[:scene/dismissed]]; with
   any other key -> []"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit core, credits.cljc, perform, the schema, or the worker"
  "No sound; no change to what the credits say"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "src/halfahead/app.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/app/enrich.cljc" "public/css/halfahead.css"
           "e2e/smoke.mjs" "src/halfahead/app/credits.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
